  "aspects": {
    "implemented": "Explicit selection/manager modes, frozen rows and positions, grouped source execution and Python bindings.",
    "verified": "365 focused Windows product cases; 23 capture-tool contracts; two native controls and six installed SDK clients per Windows/Linux platform.",
    "integrated": "Actual Analyze Measure/Measure ROIs and ROI Manager Measure all in both Windows ImGui hosts; existing jobs/leases/formatter/atomic adoption.",
    "release_ready": false
  },
  "contracts": [
    "Default AREA mode retains old area plus independent profile behavior and diagnostic version1/2 records. New modes require statistics without independent profile options; diagnostic records use version3.",
    "Manager request factory resolves stored optional T/C/Z against captured view, ordered unique indices or all stored rows, whole-plane pixel/metadata guard. Native target must match unique row positions exactly.",
    "Rows preserve requested order, while grouped execution acquires and validates each source plane once. One lookup is decoded per preparation and borrowed by line/area kernels.",
    "row_count counts returned rows; plane_count/total_pixels count distinct acquisitions. Conservative row/record/mask/kernel/output/frontend allowances refuse before source reads/callbacks.",
    "Current-line result adoption checks C/Z/T; frozen manager rows tolerate navigation/active-selection changes, but source/ROI/calibration changes reject adoption.",
    "All result rows publish atomically; pending Clear, close/cancel or later-row failure cannot append earlier rows. Scripted Measure ROIs preserves immediate results while physical UI is asynchronous.",
    "Area/thin-line scalar finite-policy UInt8/UInt16/Float32 only; line geometry includes selected plane Z in world midpoint. Names/positions/units/precision persist in independent table/CSV."
  ],
